The shared-HP ghost: a live actor the engine refuses to call

Session 20's hub runs 2 and 3 ended with one shared live key printing hp=? on both
machines, so "shared HP equal" had no pair to compare. The dump now prints WHY, and a
live run answered it in one line:

  enemykey 976CB2E9 ALIVE local=1 src=0 hp=? why=callfail seen=0 inworld=1 cls=Default_Lizer_02_C
  enemykey 93494995 ALIVE local=1 src=0 hp=490.0                     cls=Default_Lizer_07_C

Two instances of one class, one readable and one not -- so it is not the class and not the
attribute component. why=callfail means the getter resolves and the reflective call is
REFUSED, which is ObjectCallable: the item flags' deny bit (FUObjectItem::Flags bit 29,
EInternalObjectFlags::PendingKill in this build) or RF_BeginDestroyed/FinishDestroyed. In
the hub that is almost every enemy record: 565 "alive" keys, one of them callable.

So the copies the soak was trying to compare HP on were mid-teardown ghosts. The dump now
reports them as GONE -- neither ALIVE (which made the comparison unmeasurable) nor DEAD
(which would invent a kill no lane broadcast) -- and the why-line carries iflags/oflags so
the claim is a number in the log rather than an inference. `usable = live && callable`
replaces `live` for the whole per-key report, which is the same rule every reflective call
in this module already goes through.

tools/session21.ps1 gains a `probe` phase, because the harness was measuring with a
stopwatch it never checked: writing qd.enemies and reading after a fixed 3 s found the
host's dump and nothing on the peer, and the loot phase then reported "no enemy key alive
on both machines" about two machines holding hundreds. Measured: the file levers answer in
0.5-1.1 s once warm, but the FIRST dump of a boot costs 33.1 s (the per-class UFunction
resolution that makes GetHP readable is paid by whichever dump happens first). Every dump
and drop probe now polls for its lines with a real timeout.

